# Expectation record for 06_control_flow/003_switch_basic_fallthrough.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 003_switch_basic_fallthrough
area               = 06_control_flow
description        = Switch with deliberate fallthrough between labels, including through default
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
Every deliberate fallthrough carries the canonical comment that -Wimplicit-fallthrough
recognises, so the strict gate distinguishes it from a missing break.  Every accumulator
stays inside the range of int, no case label is duplicated, and each selector is an
initialized int.  Each switch is driven once by a constant and once from volatile storage.
No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a
standard-library header bcc does not ship.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
const_stacked=10 10 10 20 20 30
runtime_stacked=10 10 10 20 20 30
const_accumulate=15 14 12 8 16 32
runtime_accumulate=15 14 12 8 16 32
const_through_default=7 4 8 6
runtime_through_default=7 4 8 6
const_signed_labels=100 200 300 400
runtime_signed_labels=100 200 300 400
const_break_from_nested_block=1 1000 7
runtime_break_from_nested_block=1 1000 7
END
